; The Rust target's cram test.  It is on an alias of its OWN and not on `runtest`, because it
; needs `spectec/specs/rust` -- the PRIVATE `rust-spectec` submodule.  This repository is
; public and a public clone deinits that submodule (README, "Installation"), after which the
; encoding and its test corpus are both absent and this test could only fail.  `make test-rust`
; builds the alias explicitly and the README says so.
(cram
 (alias rust)
 (package spectec-target-rust)
 (deps
  %{bin:spectec}
  (package spectec-target-rust)
  ../../../../spectec-target-rust.install
  (source_tree ../../../specs/rust)
  (source_tree ../../../testdata/interp/rust)))
